 All notable changes to the `harness-bootstrap` package. See `references/00-overview.md` for the full package description and versioning rules (patch/minor/major, same as `skill-authoring.md`'s "Bootstrap template versioning").
 
+## 7.19.0
+
+Dev canonical skill 2.15.0 → 2.16.0. Consistency pass over the whole 7.6.0–7.18.0
+sign-off restoration, from an independent review (Fable) reading every touched file
+plus its untouched neighbors. Fixes leftover 7.5.0 "softening" language that
+contradicted the restored gates, plus unrelated stale references surfaced along the
+way.
+
+**Contradictions (would genuinely confuse an executing agent):**
+
+- `patterns/approvals.md` and `patterns/do-report-commit.md` both still said, in
+  effect, "offer a commit message and continue independent work" with no scoping —
+  read literally, license to start Step N+1 while a gated commit (Plan Step 6,
+  Implement Step 3) is still pending, i.e. the exact failure this session fixed.
+  Both now explicitly defer to a named sign-off gate's stop-and-wait when the call
+  site is one.
+- `patterns/write-confirm.md`'s entire text was the softened "no per-item
+  confirmation" version, yet Plan Step 5 names it as the mechanism for a mandatory
+  stop-and-wait. Added an explicit exception: when a call site names this pattern as
+  its sign-off gate, that gate's stop-and-wait governs, not this pattern's default.
+- `INTENT.md`'s verify checklist said "no unconditional per-file/fix/phase gates" and
+  "native Plan Mode ... or a reviewable local plan" — both are exactly the 7.5.0
+  positions this session reversed. A bootstrap installer following this checklist
+  would be told to remove the fixes. Reworded to name the fixed sign-off gates as an
+  explicit exception, and to require `EnterPlanMode`/`ExitPlanMode` unconditionally.
+- Implement's "never commit yourself" banned "any git write command", which reads as
+  conflicting with Document's `git mv` for local archival. Narrowed to specifically
+  `git add`/`git commit` (staging and committing); `git mv` for a reversible local
+  move is unaffected, same as other reversible operations elsewhere in this harness.
+  Document's own commit line reworded to state the same never-commit-yourself rule
+  explicitly, rather than the ambiguous "before any authorized commit" phrasing.
+
+**Stale references (harmless but confusing on a close read):**
+
+- `TEMPLATE.md` and every stage reference's boilerplate ("continue routine work
+  without phase-boundary confirmations" / "pause only for a concrete unresolved
+  decision or required human verification") predates the sign-off gates and reads as
+  contradicting them, even though `patterns/approvals.md`'s "explicit stop-and-wait
+  gates always win" rule already resolves it for a careful reader. Reworded both to
+  name the fixed sign-off gates as an explicit exception, so the contradiction
+  doesn't have to be resolved by cross-referencing another file.
+- `patterns/approvals.md`'s "complete all available checks first and request the
+  specific missing check" bullet is now qualified: at a sign-off gate, every plan
+  verification item is still presented regardless.
+- `templates/stat.schema.json`: `author` was required at the top level while `flags`
+  was deliberately optional, for the exact reason stated in 7.17.0's own entry
+  (required would break validation of pre-existing `stat.json` documents) — an
+  inconsistency in the schema itself, though harmless in practice since nothing in
+  `timing.mjs` actually validates against this schema file at runtime. Made `author`
+  optional too, matching `flags`.
+- `templates/report.md`'s Stage/Step Metrics table skeletons predated the 7.17.0
+  Flags column and 7.x token-coverage wording; self-healing on the first `report`
+  run, but now match the generated output for anyone reading the template directly.
+- `patterns/announce-progress.md` listed only 4 of the 6 stages in its phase-handoff
+  trigger list (missing Context Gathering and Ceremony, added by the earlier
+  6-stage restructure). `patterns/metrics.md`'s permission-allowlist example omitted
+  the `quality` subcommand that `references/06-document.md` requires before archive.
+
+All 22 existing `timing.test.mjs` cases pass unchanged; `stat.schema.json` remains
+valid JSON.
+
+## 7.18.0
+
+`docs/Engineering Guide/Documentation/01 Principles.md` (single-sourced — `docs-writer`
+doesn't duplicate this rule, so no agent file changes needed).
+
+- Softened the **Length budget** rule: it now applies to prose lines only —
+  Mermaid diagrams and tables never count against it, since they carry
+  information density prose can't match. Live-session evidence showed
+  `docs-writer` fighting the budget hard on a diagram-heavy document, treating
+  diagram lines as if they were the same cost as prose.
+- Reworded the existing split-a-companion-doc escape hatch to be something to
+  reach for readily when essential prose still doesn't fit, not a last resort —
+  the rule already permitted this, but the phrasing read as reluctant tolerance
+  rather than a normal move.
+
+## 7.17.0
+
+Dev canonical skill 2.14.0 → 2.15.0.
+
+- New **Flags** column in the Stage/Step Metrics tables (`2-report.md`) and a
+  matching `flags` array persisted on each stage/step object in `stat.json` —
+  derived, never hand-set, recalculated by `save()` on every mutation the same
+  way `metrics` already is. Surfaces 🔁 retried/rework, 🔀 scope change, 🔓
+  reopened (from existing attempt `trigger` values) and ⚠️ failed check (from
+  existing check results), so a reader can scan for problem stages/steps without
+  parsing every row or re-deriving the logic themselves from raw intervals.
+- `flags` is optional in `stat.schema.json`, not required — required would break
+  `loadState()`'s validation on every existing in-flight `stat.json` the moment
+  this ships, since older documents don't have it yet. It appears once `save()`
+  next runs.
+- Verified end-to-end: both `retried` (via `step retry`) and `failed_check` (via
+  `check record --result failed`) render correctly in both `stat.json` and the
+  rendered report table. All 22 existing `timing.test.mjs` cases still pass
+  unchanged.
